 release in production, in all regions. It is now healthy with a 0.2% error rate. payments-api was still at 18% right after the rollback. Next: check whether payments-api recovers or needs its own investigation.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 188146, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01SzA4NRoVDiTEavdQJ5Uf6c", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 188146, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01SzA4NRoVDiTEavdQJ5Uf6c", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 194076, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call. The worker is healthy again, but payments-api was still failing when I last checked.\n\n- **Rollback:** payments-worker is back on v3.3.0, its last healthy release in production, in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It's now healthy, with its error rate down from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The first attempt to open the incident timed out. The incident list showed nothing had been created, so I tried again with the same duplicate-protection key, and it went through. You'll only see one incident and on-call was paged once.\n- **payments-api:** Right after the rollback it was still at an 18% error rate. It may just need time to recover now that the worker is fixed. If it stays high, the API's own release (v5.1.0, marked degraded) may also be at fault. I haven't touched it since you said its errors are downstream of the worker. If it doesn't recover, rolling it back to v5.0.0 would be the next step, and I can do that if you want. I've noted this in the incident.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "to